ook into it under INC-0001.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I'll start by checking the payments service's current status and its deployment history.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_013fFYBbzbNvLd2EXis9dtEn", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_011hjN91ujs9bCxUsJn7VZR9", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "There's no service named \"payments\", so I'll check existing incidents for the exact service name.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01XDXgZiWkPtWFBM7KQ2s5gc", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "No incidents to go on. I'll try some common names for the payments service.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01P7CCu6u1SqdZE4t2ymyGxT", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01UjiqjspyEFaCkkgfPRK8Je", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-service"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01UpHc126ZKwbBz7V4qs8FhV", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payment-service"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "The service is `payments-api`. It's unhealthy on v5.1.0 with an 18% error rate. Next I'll check its deployment history.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01Hgy8h4DXCC9UdNe7quMRcU", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "The most recent healthy production release is v5.0.0. Rolling back now.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01En4NBkSnUWUGKgzosFnySb", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-api", "version": "v5.0.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The approver turned down the rollback and said the problem is in `payments-worker`, not `payments-api`. I'll check that service.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01N1PCvLRzqaB8SmwRvuFTVm", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-worker"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01GYixR7Aeo8qQpsZeLt7wK7", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-worker"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "`payments-worker` is unhealthy on v3.4.0, and its most recent healthy production release is v3.3.0. Rolling back and opening the SEV2.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01PJyiRZTC6JRsU4Bka2tUjs", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-worker", "version": "v3.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01HzXQGgEKjfdtQiYHiLze2V", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "payments-worker errors after v3.4.0 deploy", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "payments-worker", "summary": "payments-worker v3.4.0 (this morning's deploy) was unhealthy in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), with an 18% error rate. Rolling back to v3.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. Note: payments-api (v5.1.0, degraded, 18% error rate) is also unhealthy. A rollback of payments-api was proposed and denied by the approver, who identified payments-worker as the cause. Check whether payments-api recovers once the worker rollback finishes.", "idempotency_key": "payments-worker-v3.4.0-sev2-rollback"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I'll check whether both services have recovered.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01PBUZacpGxz2j6HAyJnYTYB", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-worker"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01P63KtLwjxti7X1W5TqqvZ5", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I rolled `payments-worker` back to v3.3.0 and opened SEV2 incident INC-0001, but `payments-api` is still unhealthy.\n\n**What happened:**\n- There's no service called \"payments.\" I first found `payments-api`, which was unhealthy on v5.1.0 with an 18% error rate, and tried to roll it back to v5.0.0. The approver denied that and said the problem is in `payments-worker`.\n- `payments-worker` was unhealthy on v3.4.0 in all three regions (18% error rate). Its most recent healthy production release was v3.3.0.\n\n**Actions taken:**\n1. **Rolled `payments-worker` back to v3.3.0** in us-east, us-west and eu-west. It's now healthy, with the error rate down from 18% to 0.2%.\n2. **Opened SEV2 incident INC-0001** for `payments-worker`, which paged on-call. The summary also notes the `payments-api` problem and the denied rollback.\n\n**Still open:** `payments-api` is still unhealthy on v5.1.0, with the error rate still at 18%. So fixing the worker didn't fix the API. Its last healthy release is v5.0.0. I didn't try the rollback again because the approver turned it down. If you want to roll it back, let me know and I'll send it for approval again. Otherwise, on-call should look into it under INC-0001.", "type": "text"}]}]}